      "definition": "Design Module Method owns generic design-contract law and an adoptable realization profile for stronger implementation discipline. It favors low coupling, modular composition, immutable typed carriers, total or nearly-total semantic transforms and explicit effects. Its goals are less ambiguity, entropy, avoidable debt, hidden authority, hidden mutation and semantic drift, greater refactorability, and preserved audit/reconstruction evidence. It concerns realization shape for module boundaries, schema/carrier families, entities/records and interfaces across languages and runtimes; it does not choose one optimal authoring path or replace SPEC_METHOD constitutional authority or ODD_METHOD graph-native law.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1,
          "quote": "# Design Module Method",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method",
          "start_line": 1
        },
        {
          "end_line": 78,
          "quote": "This method is therefore about realization design and implementation shape.\n\nIt does not mandate one optimal authoring path for every agent, worker, or\nruntime.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F1.%20Purpose",
