      "key": "design_ontology",
      "label": "Accepted Ontology"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "For governed boundary B, M(B) is the complete material-relation set of entities, identities, relationships, cardinalities, invariants, authorities and authority transitions, functions, higher-order composition laws, topology, lifecycle states/transitions, public contracts, externally observable Product meaning, declared domains/admission conditions, failure/refusal routes, effect/closure laws, projections, module mappings and material algorithmic obligations. U(B) = unresolved(M(B)). Decision completeness holds iff U(B) is empty, M(B) is jointly satisfiable, and every admitted network is semantically equivalent under governing Product, requirements and accepted design relations.",
