      "definition": "Foundation selection is a proportional, bounded comparison of candidate compositions for a material generic capability, common mechanic, algorithm or dependency. It separates irreducible semantic/authority relations and their owner, role, subject, scope, basis, lifecycle and refusal invariants from supporting generic mechanics. Candidate categories are admitted project foundations; language/runtime/platform/standard-library capability; accepted predecessor or immutable-lineage evidence; maintained external foundations where Product permits dependencies; and bounded local implementation.",
