      "definition": "The Ontology authority model records proposer, evaluator, verifier, admitter, executor, projector and retirement owner for functions/transitions crossing semantic, authority, admission, effect, persistence or public boundaries. Authority belongs in Ontology before operation shape is selected. Actor identity, available capability, attribution and domain-meaning ownership are distinct from authority, admitted current-basis capability, permission and runtime-effect ownership; proposal, evaluation, verification, admission, execution, projection and retirement remain distinct roles.",
