      "definition": "Atomic function families are the smallest parameterized families making entity lifecycles logically complete. Function-derivation evidence links discovered functionality, entity, atomic function/template, higher-order composition, effect class, required authority and disposition. Higher-order behavior names explicit composition/effect algebra and applicable identity, closure, associativity, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws. Unit/lift, sequential, parallel/applicative, fold/evaluation, retry/recovery, recursion/fixed point and projection are illustrative categories, not a required vocabulary.",
