      "key": "calculus_position_limits",
      "statement": "F1–F6 supply purpose, interpretation, identity, composition, finite-capacity and authority premises. Given explicit interpretation and typed subject, resolved compatible references on one exact basis are required before consuming a model judgment. The standard owns its additional signature, record, closure and classification choices; finite capacity and predecessor provenance do not uniquely derive them. AC-007/014 consume shared results; AC-016 consumes conjunction for claims requiring several judgments. The transformation library provides reusable responsibilities without replacing AC-013 or establishing categorical functor laws. Universal applicability, completeness, consistency, decidability, soundness and categorical status are not asserted absent the specified proof exception.",
