      "key": "calculus_scope",
      "statement": "The calculus governs symbolic-model form: identities/typed objects, exact relation endpoints, explicit constraints/latitude/residuals, traversal/judgment typing, closure/projection/overlay/transformation behavior, subject preservation and distinctions among structural, semantic and authority claims. It does not select subject vocabulary or material declarations, supply semantic acceptance, choose a carrier, execute a model or prove unique interpretation.",
