      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 398,
          "quote": "These arguments apply [F1–F6](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundational-commitments)\nto a governed symbolic model under a declared signature and interpretation.\nThe model's records represent a separately identified subject; some predicates\nadmit mechanical decision and others require semantic judgment. These are the\ncalculus's instance conditions. Its finite signature and record choices do not\nfollow from an actor's finite capacity. Selection authority remains bound by\n[Interpretation And Models](#interpretation-and-models).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#The%20STDO%20Axiomatic%20Calculus%20for%20Governed%20Symbolic%20Systems%2FFundamental%20Laws",
          "start_line": 392
        }
      ],
      "key": "fundamental_law_argument_boundaries",
      "statement": "The family arguments are conditional, not derivations of the policy inventory from finite capacity. Recoverable referents and typed joins support record admission, but closed syntax does not establish semantic adequacy; signature owners choose concrete sorts/cardinalities/domains. Context owners define scoped identity and composite-basis relations; copied/equal bytes and individually valid bases supply neither identity, transferred grants nor coherent composition. Constraint evidence retains predicate, cause, performance and effects; admission/acceptance separately require competent mandates. Uncertainty supplies neither permission nor disposition authority. Applying interpretations choose material seeds and required-edge semantics; finite unique closure must be established and is not minimum acquisition cost. Transformation owners bind equality, authorized loss and grants; resulting bytes do not admit successors or prove categorical laws. Applications choose lawful traversal topology and outer predicates. Interpretation authorities choose materiality and admitted loss; structural success cannot cure fidelity defects. Product authorities separately choose applications, carriers, acceptance and release.",
