      ],
      "key": "function_derivation_and_composition",
      "statement": "Derive the smallest parameterized families completing lifecycle. Variation only in entity/projection/transition kind, policy or subordinate payload should normally be typed parameters/closed variants rather than peers. Every evidence row is derived by admitted atom, derived by declared composition, deferred with owner/re-entry, excluded by current Product authority, or named unresolved gap. Higher-order behavior requires named composition/effect algebra and applicable identity, closure, associativity, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws rather than hidden controller flow. Iterative composition/effect/implementation discovery requires co_evolution_admissible(B); retained results reconcile into accepted design before promotion/closure. Helpers, loops, adapters and endpoints cannot become undeclared constructors.",
