    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["prime_semantic_atom", "irreducible_carrier_set", "design_ontology"],
      "conditions": [
        "Prime policy governs proposed top-level realization units."
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1083,
          "quote": "A top-level realization unit is **Prime-conformant** only when it projects one\nor more accepted Prime atoms without introducing, duplicating, or\nreinterpreting semantic authority. A topological or effect boundary must first\nbe derived and accepted as a Prime atom. Source-code size and one-to-one\ncorrespondence with an atom are immaterial.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F5.%20Prime%20Law",
          "start_line": 1079
        }
      ],
      "key": "prime_realization_conformance",
      "statement": "Derive atoms from logically complete candidate Ontology before top-level units; whole-family Prime supports Ontology acceptance. Target design/IACS/modules/functions/schemas/tests project accepted atoms and cannot originate Prime meaning. Prime-conformance covers functions, classes, carriers, top-level schema records and modules; typed closure alone does not justify a type. Units must project accepted atoms without added, duplicated or reinterpreted authority; topology/effect boundaries first require accepted atoms. Size and one-to-one correspondence are immaterial. New graph topology, typed transformation, effect, validation/admission or projection boundaries are typical lawful reasons. Mere call-site shortening, unrelated aggregation, renaming legacy interfaces, wrapper transport, hidden mutation/fallback/orchestration, nonindependent payload variants, public internal detail, near-duplicate carriers or multiplying classes for typing discomfort do not conform. Prefer composition, existing lawful functions and fewer sharper boundaries/families. The aim is avoiding semantic fragmentation/helper sprawl, not minimum line count.",
