      "key": "iacs_derivation_and_closure",
      "statement": "Derive IACS from accepted Ontology before naming subordinate payloads/modules; it should be named before helper results and branch details. Branch payload, persistence detail, read-row shape and typing convenience do not automatically justify top-level carriers. Evidence cites accepted Ontology/function derivation, declares IACS, maps every carrier to carried Ontology laws, distinguishes authoritative/downstream carriers, defaults other shapes to private subordinate payloads unless Promotion Test passes, and reconciles typed implementation before closure. IACS is a projection and cannot originate entity/function/lifecycle/authority meaning or replace Ontology. Undeclared accepted Ontology or IACS means schema not design-method complete. Co-evolution can reveal missing relations without self-ratifying; Ontology and IACS acceptance plus implementation reconciliation precede promotion/closure. Design-gated unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relations are accepted before retained implementation establishes them.",
